WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:08.965
Sunil lost forty-two thousand rupees to a fake task job. His first instinct is to block them, and delete everything.

2
00:00:09.365 --> 00:00:11.636
I just want those chats gone.

3
00:00:12.036 --> 00:00:19.110
Stop. Without evidence, there is no case. Screenshot first, block later.

4
00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:25.370
A useful screenshot shows three things: the other person's number, the date, and the time.

5
00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:33.322
Next, the UTR: the twelve-digit transaction number in the payment app. It is the fraudster's footprint.

6
00:00:33.622 --> 00:00:37.907
Keep the amount, the time, and the receiving UPI ID with it.

7
00:00:38.507 --> 00:00:47.198
For the group, note its name, the admin numbers, and the invite link. Copy links. Never click them again.

8
00:00:47.698 --> 00:00:52.867
Export the whole chat, with media, so nothing is lost if the account disappears.

9
00:00:53.467 --> 00:01:01.525
For a fake profile, save the profile link, not just the name. Names change. Links do not.

10
00:01:02.125 --> 00:01:10.755
Write everything in a simple evidence log. Keep two copies, one saved outside the phone, and never edit a saved file.

11
00:01:11.355 --> 00:01:16.514
Under the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam, electronic records are valid evidence in court.

12
00:01:17.114 --> 00:01:24.162
Collect only what is needed, with consent. Never keep or forward anyone's intimate images.

13
00:01:24.762 --> 00:01:31.003
Then upload the set on cybercrime dot gov dot in, and give the same set to the bank and the police.
